WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.546 --> 00:00:12.187
My name is Mary Chilton.

2
00:00:12.927 --> 00:00:17.308
I am one of the original Pilgrims to set sail for the New World in a ship called

3
00:00:17.328 --> 00:00:18.048
the Mayflower.

4
00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:22.310
A Pilgrim is a person who makes a journey for a religious reason.

5
00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.570
The story of the Pilgrims begins in Holland.

6
00:00:26.491 --> 00:00:29.832
Even though I am English, I was born in Leyden, Holland, in 1607.

7
00:00:32.636 --> 00:00:38.358
My family lived in Holland because we were not free to practice our religion in England, but Holland

8
00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:39.219
wasn't our home.

9
00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:41.880
It was a strange and foreign land.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.522
I lived there with my parents for 12 years.

11
00:00:46.702 --> 00:00:51.164
In 1619 we returned to England to prepare for a voyage to the New World.

12
00:00:52.044 --> 00:00:57.046
My parents and many other adults packed trunks and barrels with all the things we would need to

13
00:00:57.086 --> 00:00:58.587
begin life in the New World.

14
00:00:59.587 --> 00:01:04.738
They hired two ships, the Mayflower and the Speedwell, to take us to the New World.

15
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.482
We were all very excited and a little scared.

16
00:01:10.782 --> 00:01:17.007
We left England on August 5, 1620, but we had to return to England because the Speedwell was

17
00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:21.910
leaking. We tried to fix the ship, but it was too old and tired.

18
00:01:23.131 --> 00:01:27.834
We were forced to abandon it, leaving behind our cooking oil and some other valuables.

19
00:01:29.035 --> 00:01:30.816
We all piled into the Mayflower.

20
00:01:32.732 --> 00:01:36.713
We finally set sail for the New World on September 6, 1620.

21
00:01:38.114 --> 00:01:40.854
There were 130 people aboard the Mayflower.

22
00:01:42.015 --> 00:01:45.656
There were 102 Pilgrims and about 28 crew members.

23
00:01:46.916 --> 00:01:48.396
Three of the women were pregnant!

24
00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:54.458
It took us 66 days to reach the New World.

25
00:01:55.838 --> 00:02:01.240
Many of us became seasick when the Mayflower was tossed around by storms and strong waves.

26
00:02:02.448 --> 00:02:07.191
I spent many days being sick below deck because going above deck was dangerous.

27
00:02:09.792 --> 00:02:15.095
The wind, rain, and waves made the deck slippery, so it was easy to fall overboard.

28
00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:19.318
When it wasn't stormy and scary, the voyage was boring.

29
00:02:20.699 --> 00:02:26.682
At home I was never bored because I was busy helping my mother with the sewing, the laundry,

30
00:02:26.782 --> 00:02:27.442
or the cooking.

31
00:02:28.683 --> 00:02:33.018
But, on the Mayflower, there was very little women's work that needed to be done.

32
00:02:34.098 --> 00:02:38.321
I could have died, not from seasickness, but from boredom.

33
00:02:39.381 --> 00:02:43.543
Luckily, I had two friends, Constance Hopkins and Elizabeth Tilley.

34
00:02:44.344 --> 00:02:46.085
They made me laugh with their stories.

35
00:02:49.327 --> 00:02:53.249
Elizabeth was in love with John Howland, but he took no notice of her.

36
00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:58.632
It was both funny and sad, but never boring to watch her unrequited love.

37
00:02:59.688 --> 00:03:04.452
When we weren't listening to Elizabeth, we were often trying to avoid Francis Billington.

38
00:03:05.413 --> 00:03:07.695
He was a bully who liked to pull our hair.

39
00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:10.037
He was such a troublemaker!

40
00:03:12.178 --> 00:03:17.042
Once, he started a fire on board the Mayflower when he shot his father's gun below deck.

41
00:03:17.923 --> 00:03:21.226
Luckily, everyone heard the sound and put the fire out.

42
00:03:22.347 --> 00:03:27.691
The scariest moment aboard the Mayflower was when the ship was caught in a terrible storm for two

43
00:03:27.711 --> 00:03:28.292
whole days.

44
00:03:30.836 --> 00:03:36.400
In the single room below deck where we all lived, we huddled together and prayed to God to

45
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:36.940
save us.

46
00:03:37.921 --> 00:03:44.225
We weren't sure that God was listening, however, because on the second day of the storm, one of

47
00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.227
the main beams below deck cracked.

48
00:03:47.948 --> 00:03:53.672
Many of the sailors were scared because they knew that the ship couldn't survive another storm.

49
00:03:54.913 --> 00:03:57.174
The passengers also feared they would die.

50
00:03:58.295 --> 00:03:59.616
But God was merciful.

51
00:04:00.748 --> 00:04:04.230
No other storms caught us, and only two men died on the voyage.

52
00:04:06.451 --> 00:04:10.214
On November 9, 1620, we finally saw land.

53
00:04:11.294 --> 00:04:16.517
The ship's captain called the place Cape Cod, and he said it was many miles north of Virginia.

54
00:04:17.598 --> 00:04:24.041
We were all glad to see land after having spent 66 days in a small room with 102

55
00:04:24.141 --> 00:04:25.042
seasick people.

56
00:04:25.802 --> 00:04:31.713
We were also looking forward to breathing fresh air because the Mayflower smelled most unpleasant!

57
00:04:33.354 --> 00:04:39.917
On November 13, 1620, I was the first woman to step off of the Mayflower into the New

58
00:04:40.017 --> 00:04:43.438
World. I went ashore to help with the laundry.

59
00:04:44.498 --> 00:04:50.001
It was the only time in my life I was ever thankful to God for making laundry women's

60
00:04:50.041 --> 00:04:53.942
work, because it allowed me to stand firmly on the ground.

61
00:04:55.303 --> 00:05:01.773
We wanted to continue south to Virginia because there were other Englishmen who had settled there, but our

62
00:05:01.813 --> 00:05:03.514
attempt to sail south failed.

63
00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:08.675
The ship didn't dare go far from shore because of the damage to the beam.

64
00:05:09.615 --> 00:05:11.736
So we decided to remain in Cape Cod.

65
00:05:13.336 --> 00:05:18.838
We sent the men out to explore, and on December 12, 1620, the men returned.

66
00:05:19.778 --> 00:05:21.319
They had found a suitable place.

67
00:05:22.299 --> 00:05:24.940
They had also made contact with Native Americans.

68
00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:32.414
On December 15, 1620, we went ashore and started our new life in the New World.

69
00:05:33.315 --> 00:05:35.956
It wouldn't be an easy life, but we were hopeful.
